# crontab.example — Vulnerability Management Reporting Suite
#
# Drop-in crontab for the vuln-reports service account.
# Install as:
#   sudo -u vuln-reports crontab - < /opt/vuln-reporting/current/deploy/crontab.example
#
# Assumed install path: /opt/vuln-reporting/current  (v1.2 symlink layout)
# Runs as user: vuln-reports
#
# This is the ALTERNATIVE to the systemd daemon (deploy/vuln-reports.service).
# Use cron OR the daemon for scheduled delivery — not both at the same time.
# The daemon (systemd) hot-reloads config and manages the process; cron is simpler
# but requires the two entries below to replicate equivalent behaviour.
#
# Venv note: the lines below use the per-release venv that the updater creates
# under current/.venv/. Operators on an older hand-built install may need
# /opt/vuln-reporting/.venv/bin/python instead.
#
# After editing, verify your delivery_config.yaml with:
#   cd /opt/vuln-reporting/current && .venv/bin/python run_all.py --dry-run
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. CACHE PRE-WARMER — run before any report group fires
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# warm_cache.py pre-fetches vulnerabilities, fixed vulnerabilities, assets,
# and recast rules into parquet files so that report runs hit [CACHE HIT]
# instead of fetching live from Tenable.
#
# TIMING RULE A — schedule >=30 minutes before your earliest report group.
#   The fetch must finish before the report run starts.  If your earliest group
#   fires at 07:00 (matching the sample delivery_config.yaml), schedule this at
#   06:15 or earlier.  Adjust both times to match your actual earliest group.
#
# TIMING RULE B — NEVER schedule near midnight.
#   Cache folders are named by server LOCAL DATE (YYYY-MM-DD), not UTC.
#   If warm_cache.py fires at 23:55 and the report run fires at 00:05, the
#   date rolls over between the two and the report run will not find the cache
#   — it will re-fetch everything from Tenable, defeating the point of pre-warming.
#   Keeping this line at 06:15 satisfies both rules with comfortable margins.
#
# Adjust 06:15 to >=30 minutes before YOUR earliest delivery group.
15 6 * * * /opt/vuln-reporting/current/.venv/bin/python -m scripts.warm_cache --prune-stale >> /opt/vuln-reporting/shared/logs/warm_cache.cron.log 2>&1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. REPORT SCHEDULER — cron alternative to the systemd daemon
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# scheduler.py --mode run-due reads delivery_config.yaml, finds all groups
# whose schedule matches the current time within a +-10-minute window, runs
# those groups, then exits.  It must be called every 5-10 minutes so no
# scheduled group is missed within the matching window.
#
# This replaces the always-on systemd daemon.  Do NOT run both at the same time.
*/5 * * * * /opt/vuln-reporting/current/.venv/bin/python /opt/vuln-reporting/current/scheduler.py --mode run-due >> /opt/vuln-reporting/shared/logs/run-due.cron.log 2>&1


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. LOG ROTATION NOTE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# warm_cache.py and scheduler.py write their own rotating logs to
# shared/logs/ (warm_cache.log, scheduler.log).  The >> redirects above
# capture cron-level stdout/stderr into separate .cron.log files, which are
# NOT auto-rotated.  Add a logrotate config for them, for example:
#
#   /etc/logrotate.d/vuln-reports-cron:
#     /opt/vuln-reporting/shared/logs/warm_cache.cron.log
#     /opt/vuln-reporting/shared/logs/run-due.cron.log {
#         daily
#         rotate 14
#         compress
#         missingok
#         notifempty
#         copytruncate
#     }
#
# Reminder: adjust the warm-cache time above (06:15) and verify it is
# >=30 minutes before your earliest group in shared/delivery_config.yaml.
